course: dictionary
lesson: 14448
title: Papyrus: a plant, a paper and a document
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning is right. Papyrus can be a plant, a kind of paper, or a document written on that paper. «The papyrus grew thick along the river bank.» Here the words grew and river bank tell you papyrus is a plant.
explain: «The scribe unrolled the papyrus and began to write.» Unrolled and write are the clues. You can unroll paper, but a scribe writing on it means papyrus is the paper, not the plant. Ask yourself: is this a thing that grows, a material to write on, or a finished writing?
explain: «The museum had a papyrus that was three thousand years old.» Here the clues are museum and old, so papyrus means an ancient document. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Papyrus is a tall water plant, like a reed, that grows by the River Nile.
fact: The ancient Egyptians made a kind of paper from the papyrus plant.
fact: A papyrus is an ancient document written on this paper. The plural can be papyri or papyruses.
fact: The word «paper» comes from «papyrus».
fact: Scribes in Ancient Egypt wrote hieroglyphs on papyrus scrolls.
exercise: «The scribe wrote the message on a sheet of papyrus.» What is papyrus in this sentence? | A stone carved with pictures | *A kind of paper made from a water plant | A tall tree from the desert | A type of cloth
exercise: Where does papyrus grow? | In a dark cave | On the top of a mountain | *By the River Nile | In the desert sand
exercise: «The old papyrus scroll was found in a tomb.» Find and copy the word that tells you the scroll was made long ago. | found | *ancient | scroll | tomb
test: «Many old Bible texts were found on papyrus.» What does papyrus mean here? | A stone wall | A type of ink | *Paper made from the papyrus plant, with writing on it | A water plant with long green stems
test: Which word is the plural of papyrus, when we mean more than one ancient document? | papyrs | papyrouses | *papyri
exam: Which word comes from papyrus? | *Paper | Parrot | Pottery | Pyramid
